{#- The masthead, to the design handoff of 2026-08-02. Sticky, dark, three things in one
   row: the wordmark, a section indicator written by the homepage's scroll spy, and the
   menu button. The panel opens directly below that row.

   The handoff's panel has two columns. This site uses them for the quarterly rooms and
   the small set of permanent site pages. The grid is the handoff's auto-fit and reflows
   the same way on a phone.
   THE BRIEF column is _data/footernav.js, which is also what the footer prints, so the
   menu and the footer cannot drift apart. -#}
<header class="mast">
  <div class="mast-row">
    <a class="brand" href="{{ '/es/' if locale == 'es' else '/' }}">THE MEXICO <span class="u">BRIEF</span></a>
    {%- set Lh = uiStrings[locale] if locale else uiStrings.en %}
    <span class="mast-tag">{{ Lh.tagline }}</span>
    <div class="mast-sec" id="mast-sec" aria-live="polite"></div>
    {#- Language toggle, homepage pair only. A plain link: no JS, no cookie, no
        redirect guessing — the reader chooses, the URL says so, done. -#}
    {%- if page.url == '/' %}<a class="lang-link" href="/es/" lang="es" hreflang="es">ES</a>
    {%- elif page.url == '/es/' %}<a class="lang-link" href="/" lang="en" hreflang="en">EN</a>{% endif %}
    <button class="menu-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="menu-panel" aria-label="Menu"><span></span><span></span></button>
  </div>
  <div class="menu-panel" id="menu-panel" hidden>
    <div class="menu-grid">
      {#- The "Jump to" column of homepage anchors came out on 2026-08-03 (Alan). It was
          six links deep and only ever pointed at one page, so on every other page in the
          site it was a menu that navigated away to scroll. The homepage is short enough
          to scroll on its own. -#}
      <div class="menu-col">
        <span class="menu-h">Go deeper</span>
        {%- for group in nav %}{% if group.menu %}{% for block in group.menu %}{% for link in block.links %}
        <a href="{{ link.href }}">{{ link.label }}</a>{% endfor %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
        <a href="/about.html">About</a>
      </div>
      <div class="menu-col menu-col-quiet">
        <span class="menu-h">The brief</span>
        {%- for item in footernav %}
        <a href="{{ item.href }}">{{ item.label }}</a>{% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>
